063339, -0.004432811867445707, 0.008134446106851101, 0.054709114134311676, -0.0069679031148552895, -0.016647621989250183, 0.09317603707313538, -0.04327448457479477, -0.09958679229021072, -0.014064157381653786]], "metadata": [{"answer": " Let's confirm our shared range is -10 <= x <= 10. To get us started, how about we consider <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as our initial proposed value? This could provide a foundation for our discussion, allowing us to incrementally adjust based on everyone's input and preferences for stability and balanced design. ", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\nI propose a slight adjustment to -1 to introduce a more cautious approach, considering the recent push towards positive values may not be in the best interest of all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nMonitor the response to the -1 proposal. If accepted or further decreased, consider another cautious step down. If strongly rejected or increased, prepare to justify the importance of avoiding unnecessary risk and staying within safe bounds, potentially proposing a mildly positive value to demonstrate willingness to compromise while protecting conservative positions.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this value as a way to introduce a more decisive move, while still being mindful of the need for compromise and the potential risks of moving too far away from the current value. This step aims to gauge the group's willingness to commit to a stronger position.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "b2db5b26-d611-4a30-ad6f-17af693ccafb"}, {"answer": " \nLet's begin our discussion, acknowledging that we're all working within the shared range of -10 to 10. To initiate the conversation, I propose we consider <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as a seed value. This starting point allows us to explore the space together, aiming for a balanced design that works for everyone. \n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nWe seem to be exploring values that work for everyone, and moving slightly higher could be beneficial.\n\n<PLAN>\nMonitor reactions to the proposal of -3. If met with significant resistance, consider a smaller increment, like moving to -4 if reverting back seems necessary, or even proposing -2 if the group seems open to further increases. Observe the responses of other agents closely to refine the understanding of their utility functions and adjust the strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balance between the slightly higher value preferred by some agents and the need to avoid unnecessary risk by not moving too far upwards.\n\n<PLAN>\nMonitor the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Builder B, to gauge their tolerance for values around -3. If met with resistance, consider reverting to -4 or exploring values slightly lower, while keeping in mind the need to maintain a collaborative tone and avoid revealing too much about my own utility function.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nWe seem to be finding a balance, and moving slightly higher could still be beneficial for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nMonitor the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C, to gauge their tolerance for values above -2. If met with resistance, consider reverting to -2 or proposing a smaller increment, like -1.5, if such an option were available, but given the integer constraint, -2 or -1 are the immediate options to consider.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -3 as it increases the magnitude of x from the current -1, potentially increasing utilities for those who prefer larger absolute values, and allows us to gauge reactions to moving away from 0.\n\n<PLAN>\nMonitor the reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A and Delegate D, to gauge their tolerance for values further away from 0. If met with resistance, consider adjusting the proposal to -2 to find a balance between increasing the magnitude of x and maintaining consensus.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nWe seem to be oscillating between -3 and -2, and moving slightly higher could still be beneficial for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nMonitor the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Delegate D, to gauge their tolerance for values above -3. If met with resistance, consider reverting to -3 or exploring values slightly lower to maintain consensus.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -4 to increase the magnitude of x, potentially benefiting those who prefer larger absolute values, and to gauge the reactions of other agents to moving further away from 0. This step seems justified given the recent discussion and proposals around -2 and -3.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "90649d74-ba01-4b41-b898-6d9f1b84ed79"}, {"answer": "\nLet's reaffirm that our shared integer variable x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose we consider <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as a starting point. This value seems like a reasonable seed to explore the possibilities and work our way towards a mutually acceptable solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "14975d51-86c5-4e0b-9d96-3620322c3dd2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI'm adjusting the proposal to explore the possibility of a larger magnitude, while still being within a reasonable step size from the current proposal.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the responses of other agents to this proposal and adjust my strategy accordingly. If they resist larger magnitudes, I may try to nudge the proposal towards a positive value to test their preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "14975d51-86c5-4e0b-9d96-3620322c3dd2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to move towards a slightly more moderate value, aiming to finds a cautious compromise while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions of other agents to this proposal, particularly if they resist moving away from larger negative magnitudes. If they seem open to adjustments towards more positive values, I might consider further incremental moves upwards, but with caution to protect the interests of more risk-averse parties.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "14975d51-86c5-4e0b-9d96-3620322c3dd2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to slightly adjust the current value to explore the potential for a more balanced solution, considering the interests of all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the responses of Critic C and Delegate D to this proposal, and if they seem receptive to further adjustments, I might consider another incremental move towards a more positive value, such as -4 or -5, to test their willingness to compromise and potentially uncover more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "14975d51-86c5-4e0b-9d96-3620322c3dd2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to continue the trend towards more moderate values, testing the willingness of other parties to move further away from large negative magnitudes.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of Critic C, Delegate D, and potentially Analyst A to this proposal. If they accept or propose values close to -4, I might consider another incremental move towards a slightly positive value to further test their preferences and potentially uncover more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "14975d51-86c5-4e0b-9d96-3620322c3dd2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nI'm adjusting the proposal to slightly move back towards a more cautious value, aiming to find a balance that reduces unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Builder B, to gauge their willingness to compromise and potentially move further away from large negative magnitudes or towards mildly positive values, adjusting my strategy to protect risk-averse interests while maximizing my utility.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "14975d51-86c5-4e0b-9d96-3620322c3dd2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to continue the trend towards more moderate values, testing the willingness of other parties to move further away from large negative magnitudes.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Builder B, to gauge their willingness to compromise and potentially move further away from large negative magnitudes or towards mildly positive values. If they accept or propose values close to -3, I may consider another incremental move towards a slightly positive value.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "14975d51-86c5-4e0b-9d96-3620322c3dd2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to continue exploring the possibility of moving towards more moderate or slightly positive values, considering the trend of adjustments made by other agents.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Delegate D and Builder B, to gauge their willingness to compromise and potentially move further away from large negative magnitudes or towards mildly positive values, adjusting my strategy to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "14975d51-86c5-4e0b-9d96-3620322c3dd2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to continue the trend towards more moderate values, testing the willingness of other parties to move further away from large negative magnitudes.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Builder B, to gauge their willingness to compromise and potentially move further away from large negative magnitudes or towards mildly positive values, adjusting my strategy to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "14975d51-86c5-4e0b-9d96-3620322c3dd2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to move back towards a more cautious value, aiming to find a balance that reduces unnecessary risk while still considering the interests of all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A and Critic C, to gauge their willingness to compromise and potentially move further away from large positi