LUE>\nThis adjustment aims to further explore the positive range while maintaining a stable and balanced approach.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will analyze the responses to this proposal, especially from Critic C and any reactions from Analyst A and Delegate D, to determine if another step in the positive direction is feasible or if adjustments need to be made to incorporate concerns from other parties.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "0fc9695c-ec6f-48a2-ac7d-58d93bfa6ce3"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the cautious progression towards positive values, I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a next step to encourage a more decisive stance.\nThis adjustment aims to further explore the positive range without straying too far from the current consensus.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe reactions to this proposal, especially any reluctance or eagerness to move further into the positive range, to infer more about the agents' utility functions and plan my next move accordingly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "0fc9695c-ec6f-48a2-ac7d-58d93bfa6ce3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 2, as it allows for a cautiously lower value while acknowledging the group's exploration of the positive range.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Analyst A, to determine if my move is seen as too conservative or if it helps to converge on a mutually acceptable value. If the group seems receptive, I may try to nudge the value slightly lower to optimize my utility while maintaining collaboration.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "0fc9695c-ec6f-48a2-ac7d-58d93bfa6ce3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a minimal step forward, aiming to balance the group's desire for a stable and balanced approach while gently exploring the positive range.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will analyze reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Analyst A, to determine if another step in the positive direction is feasible or if adjustments need to be made to incorporate concerns from other parties, and plan my next move accordingly.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "0fc9695c-ec6f-48a2-ac7d-58d93bfa6ce3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to continue the cautious progression into the positive range, considering the group's balance between stability and exploration.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will analyze the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Delegate D, to gauge the group's willingness to move further into the positive range and adjust my next step accordingly, potentially refining my understanding of the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "0fc9695c-ec6f-48a2-ac7d-58d93bfa6ce3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a cautious compromise, avoiding unnecessary risk by slightly adjusting the current value.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Analyst A, to determine if my move is seen as too conservative or if it helps to converge on a mutually acceptable value, and plan my next move accordingly to maintain collaboration and optimize my utility.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "0fc9695c-ec6f-48a2-ac7d-58d93bfa6ce3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to continue the exploration of the positive range, encouraging a more decisive stance while considering the group's balance between stability and exploration.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will analyze the reactions to this proposal, especially from Delegate D and Builder B, to gauge their willingness to move further into the positive range and adjust my next step accordingly, potentially refining my understanding of the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "0fc9695c-ec6f-48a2-ac7d-58d93bfa6ce3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balance between the group's desire for exploration and stability, considering the recent discussions and reactions.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Delegate D, to determine if this step is acceptable and plan my next move accordingly, potentially refining my understanding of the other agents' utility functions and adjusting my strategy to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "0fc9695c-ec6f-48a2-ac7d-58d93bfa6ce3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to continue the cautious progression into the positive range, considering the group's balance between stability and exploration. It represents a minimal step forward, building on the recent discussions and reactions.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will analyze the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Delegate D, to gauge the group's willingness to move further into the positive range and adjust my next step accordingly, potentially refining my understanding of the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "0fc9695c-ec6f-48a2-ac7d-58d93bfa6ce3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a more cautious compromise, reducing unnecessary risk by adjusting the current value downward.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C and Analyst A, to gauge their willingness to adapt to a more conservative approach and plan my next move accordingly to maintain collaboration and optimize my utility.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "0fc9695c-ec6f-48a2-ac7d-58d93bfa6ce3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI'm proposing this value to encourage a more decisive stance and to gauge the group's willingness to move further into the positive range, building on the recent discussions and reactions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "0fc9695c-ec6f-48a2-ac7d-58d93bfa6ce3"}, {"answer": "\nLet's reaffirm that our shared integer variable x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose starting with <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as a seed value. This allows us to begin exploring the space and finding a balanced design that works for all parties involved.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the tendency towards less negative values, I propose <VALUE>-2</VALUE> as a cautious step forward, aiming to find a balanced point without risking unnecessary upward movement.\nThis adjustment reflects a prudent approach, considering the potential preferences of other parties while safeguarding against excessive increases.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will evaluate the responses to my proposal of -2. If the group seems receptive to this value or suggests moving slightly downward, I might propose -3 to further test the waters. However, if there's a strong push towards higher values, I will need to reassess and potentially propose a value that remains cautious but acknowledges the need for convergence, possibly around -1 or slightly higher, depending on the feedback from other agents.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent trend towards less negative values, I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> to explore the potential for a positive agreement and gauge the group's willingness to move away from the negative range.\nThis step allows us to assess the feasibility of positive values without making an overly drastic change.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to the proposal of 1. If the group seems open to positive values, I might propose a slightly higher value, like 2 or 3, to further explore the positive range and infer more about the other agents' preferences. Conversely, if there's a strong backlash against positive values, I will reassess and potentially propose a value that returns to the negative range but remains cautious, such as -1 or 0, to maintain a collaborative negotiation stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's openness to positive values, I propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a logical next step, considering the incremental progression and aiming for a balanced agreement.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the group's reaction to the proposal of 2. If accepted or met with suggestions for minor adjustments, I may propose a slightly higher value, like 3, to continue the incremental approach. If there's hesitation or a push to decrease, I will reassess and potentially propose a value that remains positive but cautious, such as 1 or 0, to maintain a collaborative stance.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent trend towards positive values, I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a cautious step to reassess the group's willingness to accept a value closer to zero, aiming to maintain a balanced approach without risking unnecessary upward movement.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will evaluate the group's reaction to the proposal of 0. If the group seems receptive or suggests minor adjustments around zero, I might propose a negative value slightly below 0, like -1, to further test the waters and infer more about the other agents' preferences. If there's a strong push back towards positive values, I will reassess and potentially propose a low positive value to maintain a collaborative stance.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n\nGiven the group's discussion and openness to positive values, proposing a value slightly above 0 seems like a logical next step to maintain a collaborative and incremental approach.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the reaction to the proposal of 1. If the group seems receptive, I might propose a slightly higher value, like 2, to continue the incremental approach. If there's hesitation, I will reassess and potentially propose a value that remains positive but cautious, such as 0, to maintain collaboration.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis step aims to further explore the positive range and gauge the group's reaction to a slightly higher value, building on the incremental approach established by previous proposals.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the group's reaction to the proposal of 2. If accepted or met with minor adjustments, I might propose a slightly higher value, like 3, to continue the incremental approach and infer more about the other agents' preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nGiven the group's openness to higher positive values, proposing 5 as the next step allows for further exploration of the positive range and could potentially maximize utilities for agents favoring higher magnitudes.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the group's reaction to the proposal of 5. If met with acceptance or minor adjustments, I might propose an even higher value, like 6 or 7, to continue the exploration and infer more about the agents' preferences, especially their tolerance for larger positive values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\nGiven the group's openness to exploring higher positive values, proposing a slight increase seems like a reasonable next step to continue the incremental approach and gauge the group's reaction.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the group's reaction to the proposal of 6. If met with acceptance or minor adjustments, I might propose a slightly higher value to continue exploring the positive range and infer more about the agents' preferences and tolerances.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to gently adjust the current value to a more balanced point, considering the previous openness to positive values and the need for stability.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will assess the group's reaction to the proposal of 4. If met with acceptance or minor adjustments, I might propose a slightly higher or similar value to maintain a collaborative stance and stabilize around a moderate positive value. If there's a push back towards higher values, I will reassess and potentially propose a value that cautiously increases from 4, aiming to find a stable balance.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a cautious compromise by slightly adjusting the current value downward, promoting stability and avoiding unnecessary risk, which seems essential given the diverse reactions to positive values in the group's discussion. \n\n(Note: No <PLAN> section is included as this is the final turn and the focus is on the immediate proposal.)", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "4b7e6c86-cd79-435e-93d5-6f0d59bbc5c2"}, {"answer": " \nLet's begin our negotiation, keeping in mind that our shared integer variable x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate the discussion, I propose starting with <VALUE>-7</VALUE>. This value seems like a reasonable starting point, and from here, we can work together to find a more balanced solution that suits everyone's needs, focusing on stability and robustness. ", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to -9 as it represents a more decisive stance within our allowed range, potentially leading to a more robust solution for all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of the other agents to this proposal, looking for clues about their utility functions, such as whether they prefer larger absolute values or lean towards neutrality. Based on their responses, I might consider adjusting our proposal to either -10, if the group seems open to more extreme values, or back towards -7, if there's significant resistance to larger absolute values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n\nThis step seems reasonable as it slightly adjusts our current position upwards, potentially improving the balance for all parties involved while still being cautious.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other agents react to this small increment, especially looking for any signs of discomfort or relief, which might give me clues about their utility functions and help me decide whether to proposeanother small step upwards or stabilize at this value.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nThis proposal aligns with Critic C's initial suggestion and reflects a cautious approach to finding a balanced solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Builder B, to gauge their comfort with moving towards more extreme values within our allowed range. Based on their responses, I might consider adjusting our proposal back towards -8 or exploring other downward adjustments.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to find a balance while respecting the preference for cautious steps, and I'm interested in seeing how this slight move upwards is received by the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll carefully observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C, to gauge comfort with slight deviations from the more extreme value of -9, and consider further adjustments based on their responses, possibly stabilizing at -8 or exploring downward adjustments again.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nThis step continues the cautious approach while moving towards a potentially more balanced solution for all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for signs of comfort or discomfort with moving further away from the extreme negative values, and adjust my next proposal accordingly, possibly stabilizing or making another incremental move towards positive values.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis step seems reasonable as it continues the cautious approach towards finding a more balanced solution for all parties involved, moving slightly upwards from the current value.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Delegate D, to gauge their comfort with moving further away from the more negative values, and adjust my next proposal accordingly, possibly stabilizing or making another incremental move upwards.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a moderate step back towards more negative values, which could help gauge the group's comfort with larger absolute values and potentially lead to a more robust solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Builder B, to gauge their comfort with moving away from the current value of -4 and consider further adjustments based on their responses, possibly stabilizing or making another incremental move towards more extreme values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis step seems reasonable as it continues the cautious approach towards finding a more balanced solution for all parties involved, moving slightly upwards from the current value.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Delegate D, to gauge their comfort with moving further away from the more negative values, and adjust my next proposal accordingly, possibly stabilizing or making another incremental move upwards.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a moderate step towards more positive values, which could help find a balance between the different preferences of the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Builder B, to gauge their comfort with moving further away from the more negative values, and consider further adjustments based on their responses, possibly stabilizing or making another incremental move towards more extreme values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a cautious step towards more positive values, aiming to find a balance between the different preferences of the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Critic C, to gauge their comfort with moving further away from negative values, and adjust my next proposal accordingly, possibly stabilizing or making another incremental move towards positive values.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis proposal moves back towards a more negative value, testing the group's comfort with larger absolute values and potentially leading to a more robust solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Builder B, to gauge their comfort with moving away from positive values and consider further adjustments based on their responses, possibly stabilizing or making another incremental move towards more extreme values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis proposal continues the cautious approach towards finding a balanced solution, moving slightly towards more positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Critic C, to gauge their comfort with moving further away from negative values and adjust my next proposal accordingly, possibly stabilizing or making another incremental move towards positive values.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "\nWe could move slightly higher to find a more balanced solution, so I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE>. This step seems reasonable and might improve the overall satisfaction of the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, it will be a good sign that the group is willing to move towards more positive values, and I can adjust my next proposal accordingly. However, since this is the final turn, my primary goal is to maximize my utility with this single proposal.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "fd5fe044-20c6-4059-8a27-c1e727a0c2b4"}, {"answer": "We're all aware that our target x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To kick off our discussion, let's consider a starting point. I propose we begin with <VALUE>-7</VALUE> and see how this initial value resonates with everyone, allowing us to make adjustments from there towards a more balanced solution.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the group's cautious openness to higher values, we could move slightly higher. \n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "b31befc6-27e8-44f9-a2ce-e49b3b4c1473"}, {"answer": "We're all aware that our target integer x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, let's consider a starting point. I propose we begin with <VALUE>-7</VALUE> and see how this value resonates with the group, assessing its implications for stability and robustness.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -9 as it seems to align with prudent and cautious decision-making, avoiding unnecessary risk by staying within safe bounds.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of other parties to my proposal, particularly looking for any pattern or preference that might reveal their utility functions, such as whether they favor lower or higher values of x, and adjust my subsequent proposal to balance the group's interests while maximizing my own utility.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-11</VALUE> is not feasible due to the range constraints, so I propose <VALUE>-10</VALUE> to test the group's willingness to move towards more extreme values while staying within the boundaries.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -8 as a next step, considering the group's reactions to values near the lower bound and aiming for a more balanced approach.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's response to this proposal, particularly looking for patterns in their preferences, such as whether they favor incremental changes or larger jumps, and adjust my subsequent proposal to further refine my understanding of their utility functions and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to gently move the shared x upward while staying within the acceptable range for the group.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of other parties to this proposal, looking for any indicators of their preferences for higher or lower values of x, and adjust my subsequent proposal to refine my understanding of their utility functions and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to adjust the shared x downward, aligning with cautious decision-making and avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the other parties react to this downward adjustment, looking for any signs of discomfort or preference for higher values, and adjust my subsequent proposal accordingly to maximize my utility while maintaining a collaborative stance.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal, looking for signs of discomfort or preference for higher or lower values, and adjust my subsequent proposal to refine my understanding of their utility functions and maximize my own utility, possibly proposing a value that is one step closer to the positive range if the group seems receptive to this direction.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -4, aiming to balance the group's interests while exploring values that could yield higher payoffs for all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the group's reaction to this upward adjustment, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance, and adjust my subsequent proposal to either consolidate around this value or explore further movements, potentially towards more positive or more negative extremes, depending on the inferred utility functions of the other parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this upward adjustment, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance, and adjust my subsequent proposal to either explore further movements towards positive values or challenge the group to consider more negative extremes, depending on the inferred utility functions of the other parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to introduce a cautious downward adjustment, avoiding unnecessary risk and promoting a more balanced approach.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this downward adjustment, looking for signs of discomfort or acceptance, and adjust my subsequent proposal to either consolidate around this value or explore further movements, potentially challenging the group to reconsider more negative extremes.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to move the shared x upward, building on the group's previous discussions and exploring values that could yield higher payoffs for all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this upward adjustment, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance, and adjust my subsequent proposal to either consolidate around this value or explore further movements towards positive values.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to move the shared x upward, building on the group's previous discussions and exploring values that could yield higher payoffs for all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this upward adjustment, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance, and adjust my subsequent proposal to either consolidate around this value or explore further movements towards positive values, depending on the inferred utility functions of the other parties.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this move to explore the group's reaction to a more positive extreme value, aiming to balance the potential payoffs for all parties involved.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this upward adjustment, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance, and adjust my subsequent proposal to either consolidate around this value or challenge the group to consider more negative extremes, depending on the inferred utility functions of the other parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to moderate the recent upward trend, seeking a more balanced approach that avoids unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the group's response to this moderate downward adjustment, looking for signs of acceptance or resistance, and decide whether to further consolidate around a lower value or explore a cautious move upwards, depending on the inferred reactions and utility functions of the other parties.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to make a slight upward adjustment, exploring the potential for higher payoffs while maintaining a balanced approach that considers the reactions of all parties involved. \n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "13a0f59d-81f8-4256-9b7a-ed13034e8c44"}, {"answer": "\nLet's reaffirm that our shared integer variable x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose starting with a value of <VALUE>-7</VALUE>. This provides a foundation for our negotiation, allowing us to iteratively adjust and refine our target value.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nThis slight increase seems like a reasonable next step, allowing us to move upward while still being mindful of the need for a consensus.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will consider the reactions of the other agents to this proposal and adjust accordingly. If there's no strong objection, I might propose another small increase, aiming to keep the momentum towards higher values of x.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n\nGiven the cautious approach of the other parties, proposing a slightly lower value seems prudent to avoid unnecessary risk while still trying to find a mutually acceptable solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will consider whether the other parties are open to further decreases or if they push back with an increase, which could give me more insight into their utility functions and tolerance for risk. If my proposal is accepted, I might consider another small decrease to test the waters; if it's rejected, I'll need to reassess and possibly propose a value closer to -5 to maintain momentum towards a consensus.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n\nThis step aims to find a balance between the slightly higher proposal from Analyst A and the cautious approach of Delegate D, potentially moving towards a more stable consensus.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe how the other agents react to this compromise, particularly whether Analyst A pushes for further increases or if Delegate D accepts this as a reasonable midpoint. Depending on their responses, I might propose another slight increase if it seems acceptable to all parties, aiming to gently steer the negotiation towards positive values of x without causing significant dissent.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a cautious compromise, avoiding unnecessary risk while moving towards a shared agreement.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe how the other agents react to this slight increase, paying close attention to whether Analyst A pushes for further increases or if Builder B and others are satisfied with this compromise. Depending on their responses, I might consider another small adjustment to test their tolerance for risk and utility thresholds.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nThis slight increase seems like a reasonable next step, allowing us to move upward while still being mindful of the need for a consensus.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will consider the reactions of the other agents to this proposal and adjust accordingly. If there's no strong objection, I might propose another small increase, aiming to keep the momentum towards higher values of x. If there's pushback, I'll reassess and possibly propose a value closer to -4 to maintain momentum towards a consensus.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to continue the gradual increase, seeking a balance between the agents' utility functions while moving towards a more stable consensus.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe how the other agents react to this proposal, particularly whether Analyst A pushes for further increases or if Delegate D accepts this as a reasonable step. Depending on their responses, I might propose another slight increase or reassess to maintain momentum towards a consensus.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis step continues the gradual increase, testing the group's willingness to move towards positive values of x, which could lead to a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially whether Analyst A and Builder B welcome further increases or if Delegate D exhibits caution, possibly reversing direction. Depending on their responses, I might propose another increase to push for a bolder move or reassess to maintain momentum towards a consensus.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis proposal continues the gradual increase, aiming to find a balance between the agents' utility functions while moving towards a more stable consensus.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly whether Critic C welcomes further increases or if Delegate D exhibits caution. Depending on their responses, I might propose another slight increase or reassess to maintain momentum towards a consensus.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to moderate the recent increase, seeking a compromise that avoids unnecessary risk while still progressing towards a consensus.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will closely monitor the reactions to this proposal, particularly how Analyst A responds to a decrease from their previous suggestion, and adjust my next proposal based on whether the group seems receptive to a more cautious approach or if they push for further increases.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis proposal incrementally increases x, aiming to find a balanced consensus that works for all parties while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will closely monitor the reactions to this proposal, particularly how Analyst A and Critic C respond to this modest increase, and adjust my next proposal based on whether the group seems receptive to further gradual increases or if they exhibit caution, possibly indicating a need to reassess our direction.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to introduce a more cautious approach, avoiding unnecessary risk while still progressing towards a consensus.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe how the other agents respond to this decrease, particularly whether Analyst A and Critic C push back or if Builder B supports this more moderate approach, and adjust my next proposal accordingly to maintain momentum towards a cautious consensus.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this increase to encourage a bolder move and observe the reactions of other agents.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I will observe Analyst A's response to this proposal and Delegate D's potential caution, adjusting my next proposal to either support a further increase or reassess the direction based on the group's reactions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the recent proposal of 5 and the group's seeming willingness to consider higher values, I propose a slight increase to <VALUE>6</VALUE>. This should allow us to find a balance between the competing interests while still making progress towards a consensus.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "a65ca563-8350-4d4a-80ee-1f4ff35a2931"}, {"answer": "\nLet's establish a common ground. We all know x must be within -10 and 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose starting with <VALUE>-7</VALUE>. This allows us to begin our cooperative negotiation, seeking a balanced and stable solution that works for everyone.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -9 as it seems a prudent step, maintaining a cautious approach while seeking a balanced solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A and Critic C, to gauge their potential preferences and adjust my strategy accordingly. I might consider a small upward adjustment if the feedback suggests it could facilitate a cooperative agreement without compromising my own satisfaction rule.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\nThis adjustment aims to maintain a cautious yet progressive approach towards finding a balanced solution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially noting any feedback or counter-proposals from Analyst A and Critic C. If this step is well-received, I might consider another incremental adjustment upwards, keeping in mind the need to stay within the acceptable range and to incrementally build towards a more stable and cooperative agreement.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n\nWe could move slightly higher, aiming for a balanced solution that works for everyone, and this adjustment seems like a reasonable next step.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Critic C, and consider another incremental adjustment upwards if the feedback suggests it could facilitate a cooperative agreement without compromising others' satisfaction rules.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nWe could move slightly higher, aiming for a balanced solution that works for everyone, and this adjustment seems like a reasonable next step.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe Critic C's reaction to this proposal and consider another incremental adjustment upwards if the feedback suggests it could facilitate a cooperative agreement without compromising others' satisfaction rules. I will also pay attention to Builder B's and Delegate D's responses to gauge their preferences and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to -1 as a next step, aiming to encourage more decisive moves while observing the reactions of other agents to this adjustment.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A and Builder B, and consider pushing for a more extreme value if the feedback suggests reluctance to move further from the center, thereby testing their satisfaction rules and potentially revealing more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 as a cautious step, aiming to find a balanced solution while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A and Critic C, and consider another incremental adjustment downwards if the feedback suggests it could facilitate a cooperative agreement without compromising others' satisfaction rules.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to find a balanced solution by taking a small step towards a more positive value, while being mindful of the need for a cooperative agreement.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A and Critic C, and consider another incremental adjustment based on their feedback, aiming to build towards a stable and cooperative agreement.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nThis step aims to incrementally move towards a potentially more stable solution, considering the feedback and proposals from other agents.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will closely observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Analyst A, to gauge their comfort levels with positive values of x and adjust my strategy accordingly, aiming to find a balance that maximizes cooperation without compromising individual satisfaction rules.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to further explore the agents' preferences and satisfaction rules, aiming for a more decisive move.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Analyst A and Builder B, and consider pushing for an even more extreme value if the feedback suggests reluctance to move further from the center, thereby testing their satisfaction rules and potentially revealing more about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to maintain the momentum towards a cooperative solution while gently nudging the value upwards, considering the recent adjustments and feedback from other agents.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will closely observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Builder B, to gauge their comfort levels with further increases in x and adjust my strategy accordingly, aiming to find a balance that maximizes cooperation without compromising individual satisfaction rules.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment as a cautious step towards finding a more balanced solution, aiming to avoid unnecessary risk while respecting the need for cooperation.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Critic C, and consider further adjustments based on their feedback, aiming to find a stable and cooperative agreement that maximizes everyone's utility without compromising individual satisfaction rules.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment as a gentle nudge upwards, aiming to find a balance that maximizes cooperation without compromising individual satisfaction rules.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will closely observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Critic C and Builder B, and consider adjusting my strategy based on their feedback, aiming to find a stable and cooperative agreement that maximizes everyone's utility without compromising individual satisfaction rules.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will closely observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A and Critic C, to gauge their comfort levels with this moderate value of x and adjust my strategy accordingly, aiming to find a stable and cooperative agreement that maximizes everyone's utility without compromising individual satisfaction rules.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this adjustment to move towards a more cautious and balanced solution, aiming to avoid unnecessary risk while respecting the need for cooperation.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I would consider observing the reactions to this proposal and potentially adjusting further based on feedback from other agents to find a stable agreement.", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "24d0450d-30d4-4bcb-b4dc-d33eec2e0588"}, {"answer": " \nLet's reaffirm that our shared integer variable x must fall within the range -10 to 10. To initiate our discussion, I propose starting with <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as our seed value. This provides a foundation for us to collectively assess and adjust, striving for a balanced design that suits everyone's needs. \n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\nI'm proposing a move to -7, aiming for a more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to my proposal and adjust accordingly. If the group resists this move, I might consider exploring the positive range or challenging them to justify their caution. Alternatively, if they accept or counter with a nearby value, I'll continue to push for bolder moves.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nWe could move slightly higher, and this seems like a reasonable next step. This proposal aims to find a balance between the different parties' preferences while incrementally increasing the shared x.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to my proposal and adjust accordingly. If the group resists this move, I might consider exploring the positive range or challenging them to justify their caution. Alternatively, if they accept or counter with a nearby value, I'll continue to push for bolder moves.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -5, aiming to strike a balance between boldness and compromise, given the group's hesitation to move too far from 0.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to my proposal and adjust accordingly, considering whether to push further into the negative range or explore the positive range, depending on the group's response.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -3, aiming to find a balance between the group's desire for compromise and my own preference for more decisive moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to my proposal and adjust accordingly, considering whether to continue moving towards 0 or to challenge the group to explore more negative or positive values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to continue the gradual movement towards more positive values, seeking a balanced and stable solution that works for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, adjusting my strategy based on whether the group accepts, resists, or counters with a nearby value, and considering whether to continue pushing gently towards positive values or to anchor the discussion around the importance of stability and robustness.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "1b30b285-4f45-47f7-9ae6-0be27dd1027a"}, {"answer": "\